            <ArticleTitle>[Isolated neurosarcoidosis without systemic signs].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>455-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Sarcoidosis is a multisystemic disease which involves the nervous system in 5 to 15 p.cent. Neurosarcoidosis without signs of systemic disease is rare and may be difficult to diagnose. We report a case of a 61 year-old patient with a pseudotumoral neurosarcoidosis and along evolution of 25 years without systemic signs. In such cases, histological analysis is rewarding.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
